        "title": "Randomized controlled trial on ovarian and tubal cancer screening",
        "description": "Enrollment: 202638 participants; Study design: randomized controlled trial; Setting: 13 centers in National Health Service trusts in England, Wales, and Northern Ireland; Follow-up duration: 16.3 years; Allocation concealment: The trial management system confirmed eligibility and then randomly allocated women using the Visual Basic randomisation statement and the RND function; Blinding: Investigators and participants were aware of group allocation, but members of the outcomes committee were masked to the randomization group; Intention-to-treat: Yes; Funding source: National Institute for Health Research, Cancer Research UK, and The Eve Appeal",
